  "scope": "# Bounded foundation-history follow-up\n\nThe previous common-One bridge pilot remains closed negative. This asks one\nremaining question:does the curriculum work better when the model already\nlearned to use recurrence during pretraining? It is an explicitly adaptive\nfollow-up on consumed discovery DEV,not independent confirmation or a repair\nthat changes the old result.\n\n## Foundations and controls\n\nRetain original scientific seed5231 checkpoints from the same random initializer:\nR at1.004887590B targets;One at the same source exposure;and the stronger One at\n1.237788282B targets,approximately matched to R's retained pretraining work.\nVerify complete original states/roles,digests and equal prediction inventory.\nRemove only the closed training-only head;reset every adaptation optimizer.\nNever adopt a fitted qualification or previous curriculum state.\n\nExecute seven cooled endpoints:One-work/NTP andOne-work/bridge;R/NTP andR/bridge;\nOne-source/NTP andOne-source/bridge;plus a longer One-work/bridge control. The\nbasic arms receive200 updates. The longer One endpoint is245 updates,computed\nfrom the complete retained pretraining-plus-adaptation matrix budget before\nthis study. That leaves0.00961% unused full-trajectory work;the next update\nwould exceed it. Retained update trajectories are separate from prior tuning,\ndiscarded branches and total development receipts,which remain preserved.\n\nAll basic continuations see identical128-window NTP updates beginning at source\nwindow1,210,880,beyond every parent's cursor. R andOne-source did not consume the\nintervening One-work pretraining targets. Their entire source histories match;\nOne-work's longer history is the resource control. This new shared slice differs\nfrom the old pilot,so cross-study changes are not a pure causal history estimate.\n\n## Fixed learning and execution\n\nKeep the identical1,618 original worked problems,view construction,task order\n(seed40009),noise policy,ordered normal-decoder loss and curriculum. Each bridge\nupdate uses128 original task views and128 NTP windows. Loss is mean source NTP\nplus0.3 mean original-answer CE plus0.03 per-example artificial task-EOS CE.\nAll original math text/steps/answers remain source substrings;no calculator\nlabels,teacher model,generated examples or RL. First quarter shows all original\nwork,second quarter its first half,final half none. Keep ordinary NTP throughout.\n\nOne always uses one pass;R cycles4,1,2 synchronized terminal passes with full\nbackpropagation. Same0.001 peak LR,10-update warmup,half-endpoint cooldown to\n10% of peak;no HPO or additional rate/weight/depth/epoch search. The longer One\ngets its own245-update curriculum/cooldown and may share only the identical\nfirst stable update with its200-update parent. Never extend a cooled endpoint.\n\nFreeze exact sources,data,parents,endpoints and ports before updates. Every\nbasic case first stops after one actual registered update. Require independent\npinned-upstream FP32 complete128-window NTP and applicable128-task gradients,\nall families within2%,component loss agreement0.003 and independent clipping/\noptimizer/moment checks. Count first updates as research even if a gate fails.\nOnly then continue from exact model/optimizer/per-rank RNG restoration. Verify\nall32 replicas and complete source/task/matrix counters. Bit-exact future\ntrajectories are not assumed. Record100 actual warm updates20\u2013119.\n\nUse all16 chips as two owned eight-chip jobs when ready. Existing measured\nwarm updates take0.39\u20130.61s;reserve2s/update plus launch/CPU overhead. Overall\ncap7,200s,native/CPU phases1,200s. Preserve512GiB MemAvailable,35GiB free and\n10,000 inodes. Include all failures,compiles,first-update gates and CPU tails.\nDo not extend the clock or stop a scientific arm because of an unfavorable score.\n\n## Frozen readouts and stopping\n\nFinish all seven fits before any held-out follow-up readout. Use the exact\n135-task/115-group consumed discovery panel,no-work prompts,prefix-only fixed\nnoise,24-token greedy budget,EOS requirement and whole-scalar verifier. One\nuses1;R reports1,2,4,with2 the predeclared operating point. Independently audit\nwhole-panel answer NLL in FP32. Score every model on the common consumed natural\nDEV curve cohort,all original targets and60/20/20 domain weights.\n\nThe single primary domain contrast is R/bridge depth2 against the fully work-\nmatched longer One-work/bridge depth1. Retain the5pp useful domain screen and\nconditional paired source-group intervals. Report source-matched and equal-\ncontinuation controls,the objective interactions,and same-R supported1\u21922\naccuracy separately. No exit selection or confidence from one training pair.\nThe original0.01-nat broad-source criterion remains unchanged. No domain result\ncan complete the broad goal,spend terminal alpha or replace fresh confirmation.\n\nIf this bounded history comparison also lacks useful held-out generalization\nand supported-pass benefit,close this bridge family at this scale. No additional\ncurriculum sweep or automatic scaling. If promising,independent fresh-source/\nseed confirmation,strong tuned controls and inference-cost comparisons remain\nrequired. No new TEST/reserve access. Old negative results remain visible.\n",
